.TH B34ST 1 "June 2026" "B34ST 0.4.2b" "Operator Tools"
.SH NAME
B34ST \- guided control plane for FBR34KER research workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B B34ST
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B B34ST
is the canonical operator entry point for the project. With no arguments it
opens a session-logged guided control panel covering builds, tests, QEMU,
external authorized first-stage execution, FBRI images, next-stage loading,
deployment, modules, runtime console access, modification evidence, physical
validation, and release packaging.
.PP
Firmware workflows include target-specific IPSW discovery, Apple-hosted
downloads, signed update or erase-restore execution, and tethered downgrade
plans delegated to an external authorized boot adapter.
.PP
The ramdisk maker/loader resolves an exact iPhone, iPad, or Apple silicon Mac
profile, records the exact OS/build, creates a deterministic hash-verified
FBRD from prepared components, and produces a plan-only load request. Physical
loading requires a separately installed target/build-specific adapter. See
.IR docs/RAMDISK_MAKER_LOADER.md .
.PP
For an unsigned target, select
.B Guided tethered downgrade.
The guide chooses a local or catalog-downloaded IPSW, validates the exact
product and manifest, saves a readiness plan, preflights a separately installed
external adapter, and only then offers execution. B34ST does not bundle the
target-specific adapter. Without one, the guide stops safely after planning.
The external tethered boot must run again after every device restart.
.PP
The tether adapter is a separately installed, target-specific executable: a
program, script, or reviewed wrapper around device boot tooling. It communicates
with the device in DFU/recovery mode and performs the external boot sequence.
It is not the IPSW, USB cable, idevicerestore, or a universal B34ST component.
B34ST validates and orchestrates; the adapter performs the device-side boot
work and returns structured JSON.
.PP
Public checkm8-era projects such as Legacy iOS Kit, Semaphorin, and palera1n
target A11 or earlier hardware and are not drop-in adapters for B34ST's current
A12+ profiles. futurerestore uses a separate SHSH/SEP/baseband restore model.
See the compatibility table in
.IR docs/TETHERED_DOWNGRADE.md .
.PP
The initial dashboard displays the connected product, mode, board, reviewed
launch firmware, current firmware when available, latest signed firmware,
matching profiles, and device-specific available or blocked actions.
.PP
Target-changing operations require explicit authorization. Runtime
modification and jailbreak states are evidence-gated and are not inferred
from transport success or textual monitor output.
.PP
The installed executable uses uppercase
.B B34ST
because the source package directory is named
.IR b34st ;
case-insensitive filesystems cannot safely provide both names.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B control-panel
Open the guided operator interface.
.TP
.B research-runtime
Run the exact-target, evidence-gated physical research-runtime orchestrator.
.TP
.B environment-plan
Create a bounded simulation or research-runtime plan.
.TP
.B validate-session
Validate a recorded session bundle.
.TP
.B physical-validation
Generate or inspect physical-validation evidence.
.TP
.B hardware-prepare
Generate read-only hardware preparation material.
.TP
.BI "fbr34ker " arguments
Run a lower-level FBR34KER backend command.
.SH TETHERED DOWNGRADE ADAPTER
Set
.B B34ST_TETHER_ADAPTER
to the reviewed adapter executable and arguments, or enter the command when
prompted. The adapter reads one request JSON object on standard input and
writes one response JSON object containing
.B {"ok": true}
or
.B {"ok": false, "error": "..."}
to standard output. See
.I docs/TETHERED_DOWNGRADE.md
and
.I schemas/tethered-downgrade-adapter-v1.json.
.SH RAMDISK ADAPTER
Set
.B B34ST_RAMDISK_ADAPTER
to the reviewed target/build-specific adapter executable and arguments.
The load operation is plan-only unless execution, owner authorization, and
the separate load confirmation are explicit. See
.I docs/RAMDISK_MAKER_LOADER.md
and
.I schemas/ramdisk-adapter-v1.json.
.SH SOURCE TREE
From the unpacked source tree, run:
.PP
.RS
.B ./scripts/B34ST
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbr34ker (1)
